Geometry, time scale and the range of a model (@em-scales: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @electromagnetism, #source "../sources/Electromagnetics-Volume-1-Ellingson.lingua#r_30KS80JAJY91W0FGZMASQW9DJA", #source "../sources/Electromagnetic-Fields-and-Energy-Haus-Melcher.lingua#r_1VKHEEC14B3VDGBA13T6K4JQNV", #electromagnetism "../../../../inquiry/quantitative-literacy/foundations/Units-and-dimensions.lingua#r_3A511KGNX59K2YHKT83NM38NE1") { r_4WAT0ASSD1WYXGBDTKWTFWZ7VZ
**Read:** [Electromagnetics Volume 1 — Steven W. Ellingson](../sources/Electromagnetics-Volume-1-Ellingson.lingua#r_30KS80JAJY91W0FGZMASQW9DJA), chapters 1–2 in full; [Electromagnetic Fields and Energy — Haus and Melcher](../sources/Electromagnetic-Fields-and-Energy-Haus-Melcher.lingua#r_1VKHEEC14B3VDGBA13T6K4JQNV), introductory field and quasistatic developments.

A field description depends on spatial resolution, time scale, material state and the desired observable. A copper wire can be treated as a lumped resistance at one frequency, a transmission structure at another, and an electron-scattering problem at a smaller scale. These are related descriptions with different omitted effects.

Compare apparatus dimension L with wavelength λ and propagation time L/v with the time over which the source changes. A small L/λ supports a quasistatic approximation but does not alone establish negligible losses, uniform current or an ideal ground. Compare conductor dimensions with skin depth; compare the response time of the material with the signal time. An electrostatic solution assumes time-independent charge and suitable equilibrium, not the absence of all microscopic motion.

For each problem record geometry, excitation, material law, boundary/initial conditions, units and the observable. Then list neglected phenomena and a test that could expose one. An uncertainty interval on a calculation cannot repair an unsuitable model. The later records develop electrostatic, magnetostatic, quasistatic, wave, radiation and material descriptions without treating their boundaries as walls between subjects.

